WEBVTT

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:16.380
If I fell, it'd pretty much be game over!

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:20.670
You've made a really
dangerous puzzle here!

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.170
Hey! Mr. Galileo, aka Gammon!

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.450
I'm pleased that you're enjoying it!

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.180
That makes having put my all
into creatin' it worthwhile.

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:33.180
As a Giver for the POG, that is!

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:36.100
So you're the POG's body and soul, huh?

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:39.110
Making a damn Puzzle of Fools again!

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:40.710
Puzzle of Fools?

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:42.230
You're wrong.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:43.760
I made this specially to

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.490
send you straight to Hell:
a Puzzle of Death!

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:49.490
I'm droppin' three beams.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:05.430
I won't let puzzles be
used to kill people!

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:06.630
Never!

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.180
It's your life that's in danger, man.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:12.180
You're as dumb as always.

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:18.820
Well, let's have fun with our
deadly puzzle time, Einstein!

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:42.830
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:45.620
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:47.410
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:50.170
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:54.670
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:59.390
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:01.600
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:04.260
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:06.270
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:08.560
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:10.520
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:13.320
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:17.860
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.110
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:24.790
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:27.040
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:29.370
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:32.000
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:37.880
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:43.550
Brain diver

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:48.310
Brain diver

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.940
The Speeding Challenger

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:02.540
Delicious!

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:04.160
It's so delicious!

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:07.290
There's lots of it, so
have plenty more, okay?

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:10.050
What's wrong?

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:16.180
I'm able to eat this delicious food

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:19.180
because you were kind enough
to say something to me!

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:23.310
Thank you so much, Miss Nonoha!

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:26.020
I owe you my life!

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:28.560
My brother threw me away,
but you came and picked me up!

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:33.270
I don't think Gammon
threw you away, Miharu.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:35.320
Gammon...

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:38.070
Master Rook gave him an offer.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:41.580
And it was Galileo himself who accepted.

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:44.580
Gammon's gone over to the POG...

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.500
Come on, eat.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:53.300
You can stay over here tonight.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.580
Thank you very much!

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:02.110
You're a good eater.

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:04.080
You're not even leaving any leeks.

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:06.110
I love leeks!

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:09.110
I'm glad I gave dinner my all.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:12.730
Still...

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:15.860
Where's he running around
at so late at night?

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:17.970
Mr. I-Hate-Onions?

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:19.110
Kaito,
It's dinner with Miharu!
When you get back,
drop by my place.
Come on!
Nonoha

00:04:20.770 --> 00:04:21.870
I'm dropping one beam.

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:28.740
I'm doin' three.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:48.150
Mr. Galileo certainly is being forceful.

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:52.030
Still, this puzzle he's thought
up is impressive, isn't it?

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:55.350
You can remove up to three
metal beams at once.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:57.760
The winner is whoever drops the last beam

00:04:57.760 --> 00:04:59.350
on which his opponent stands.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:02.710
Like a three-dimensional
game of checkers.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:04.400
I guess you could say.

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:07.530
It's nothing that simple.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:10.590
All beams not connected
to the puzzle frame

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:12.050
will fall to the ground.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:16.140
In other words, depending
on which beams you drop,

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:18.300
you can knock several
others down at once.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:21.570
Not only is this three-dimensional,

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:24.150
there are countless ways to attack and drop beams.

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:27.310
This is an incredible,
high-level competitive puzzle.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:31.310
What's more, you only have one minute
to think of your turn.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:33.320
I'm pissed off, but...

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:34.870
This is an interesting puzzle!

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:38.590
And that makes me even more pissed off!

00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:41.080
That this puzzle's being
used to kill people!

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:49.490
Do you know what you're doing?!

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:52.590
Don't you have any shame,
bein' led around by money?

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:54.050
Money?

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:56.680
You're still talkin' that stupid BS?

00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:59.180
I don't care about money anymore!

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:01.220
I'm after somethin' way better!

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:04.690
I'm gonna solve the Puzzle of God

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:07.850
and get the ultimate
prize, the Book of God!

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:09.080
Gammon!

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:11.600
You mean, that's why you joined the POG?!

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:14.060
That friggin' unbelievable
prize will give

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:16.610
whoever gets it ultimate power.

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:18.680
The Book of God!

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:22.080
It's sealed up inside the Puzzle of God,

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:24.490
which no one has been able to solve.

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:26.120
Givers and Solvers alike,

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:28.020
there ain't no one who don't want it!

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:30.750
Do it, Kaito! Use the armlet's power!

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:32.000
What?!

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:35.460
This battle is gonna prove
once and for all that,

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:37.630
even if you use that, you still can't beat me!

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:39.300
And then...

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:48.930
I'll prove that I'm the real Phi-Brain!

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:50.890
Dream on.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:55.030
There's no way I'm losin'
to a prick like you!

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:06.910
What's the matter?

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:09.410
If you don't use the armlet,
this is all you've got?

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:11.170
Shut the hell up.

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:13.420
Even without the armlet,

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:15.920
I can solve this puzzle, no problem!

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:21.930
I see it.

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:24.180
If I release those two beams...

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:54.000
Wh..What is this?

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:07.810
Kaito!

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:10.490
What are you zonin' out for?!

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:12.180
Hurry up and go!

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:13.810
Shut up!

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:18.320
What was that just now?

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:20.250
I'm sure of it.

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:23.020
If I drop those two beams, I'll win.

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:25.660
But...

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:31.660
that's what will happen?

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:42.050
You're almost out of time, Kaito Daimon!

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:44.430
Dammit! Okay, fine!

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:45.550
I'll drop this one beam!

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:53.980
You made a dumb-ass mistake, Einstein!

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:56.100
I've seen it: the end of you!

00:08:57.230 --> 00:08:58.360
One.

00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:03.360
Two.

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:15.970
This is the finishing move!

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:22.320
That's far enough!

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:31.960
I have orders from Master Rook:

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:34.390
Leave from here, Galileo-Gammon!

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:36.850
Huh?! Quit screwin' around!

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:38.150
With just one turn, this guy will-

00:09:38.150 --> 00:09:40.480
If you are a member of the POG,

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:42.780
Master Rook's order is absolute!

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:44.470
Rook...

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:49.660
He saved your skin, Einstein!

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:09.260
Brother...

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:10.870
Leeks...

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:24.020
Awesome! You're really awesome!

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:28.570
I never thought you could
drive Kaito Daimon that far!

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:30.770
Still, I thought you were awesome

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:33.540
right from the start, Mr. Gammon!

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:36.530
This tea sucks.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:38.870
Hey, you didn't make it right!

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:41.710
My humblest apologies.

00:10:41.710 --> 00:10:43.790
I am unfamiliar with the making of tea.

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:46.700
A guy like this, treated as an executive?

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:48.170
It makes no sense!

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:50.120
He produced results.

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:51.930
We have to accept it.

00:10:51.930 --> 00:10:54.550
I can't accept it!

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:57.440
Rook was the one who told
me to kill Kaito Daimon.

00:10:57.440 --> 00:10:58.770
Why'd he stop me?

00:10:58.770 --> 00:11:00.480
A change in plans.

00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:04.170
Once we know you can be trusted
as a member of the POG,

00:11:04.170 --> 00:11:06.190
you will be informed of the details.

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:08.860
Oh, yeah?

00:11:09.210 --> 00:11:12.640
But the next puzzle ain't
goin' down this way!

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:14.130
Before you can stop me,

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:16.120
I'm gonna
send that guy straight to Hell!

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:26.800
His actions were more than we expected.

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:29.160
Gammon Sakanoue...

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:32.540
If you hadn't stopped him, Master Rook,
Kaito Daimon would have...

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:36.560
If he had defeated Kaito Daimon,

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:38.930
the title of Phi-Brain would have-

00:11:38.270 --> 00:11:38.930
There.

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:44.810
The Artmlet of Orpheus is reacting
in a way it never has.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:48.690
Proof that Kaito's brain
was suddenly stimulated.

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:51.740
You mean, the armlet was activated?

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:57.250
That reaction is him unconsciously
drawing on the armlet's power.

00:11:57.250 --> 00:11:59.630
He is close to being
a perfected Phi-Brain.

00:12:00.050 --> 00:12:01.440
But...

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:02.960
one thing troubles me.

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:06.220
If the armlet was activated,

00:12:06.220 --> 00:12:09.260
I don't think Kaito Daimon would
have been so easily defeated.

00:12:09.260 --> 00:12:10.260
Perhaps...

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:14.860
there is some reason
that he could not win.

00:12:14.860 --> 00:12:16.000
Who can say?

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:20.910
All we know is that Kaito
has most definitely grown.

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:23.130
Gammon Sakanoue...

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:26.240
He will no doubt become
the greatest piece.

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:29.240
For the purpose of opening
Kaito's "door," that is.

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:33.020
I shall continue to
monitor Gammon Sakanoue

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:37.200
until we can confirm his
allegiance to the POG.

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:38.340
Yes.

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:45.460
Kaito has begun to speed forward.

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:50.590
Soon, you will no longer
be able to stop him.

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:20.930
Kaito!

00:13:20.930 --> 00:13:23.940
Kaito, where'd you go last night?

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:25.540
I left you a note, didn't I?

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:27.290
That I'd made dinner?

00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:28.560
I didn't see it.

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:31.770
Jeez! Miharu and I waited for you!

00:13:31.770 --> 00:13:34.860
Ah, Miharu really is cute.

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:38.350
Hard to believe she's
Gammon's sister, huh?

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:42.410
Maybe she'll keep living with me
till Gammon comes back.

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:45.990
What's the matter, Kaito?

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:47.530
Ain't no way she would.

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:50.440
Well, now, seems you're getting along
first thing in the morning.

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:52.440
Upperclassman Jikukawa?

00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:56.030
Still, there was a piece
of unpleasant news.

00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:57.810
Kaito...

00:13:57.810 --> 00:14:01.030
Last night, you battled
a POG puzzle, didn't you?

00:14:01.810 --> 00:14:04.410
The Giver was Gammon Sakanoue.

00:14:06.340 --> 00:14:07.850
I was quite surprised.

00:14:07.850 --> 00:14:11.290
To think, he's joined with
Director Crossfield...

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:14.360
I'm sure that's why he's
not at school anymore.

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:17.200
So, Kaito wasn't in last night because...

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:21.260
Yes, he was challenging Gammon's puzzle.

00:14:21.470 --> 00:14:22.550
And...

00:14:22.890 --> 00:14:23.640
Yes?

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:27.090
What?!

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:28.950
Who the hell beat you before

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:30.980
we could defeat you, Kaito Daimon?!

00:14:31.480 --> 00:14:32.500
That's right!

00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:34.610
Revamped each time they were beaten,

00:14:34.610 --> 00:14:36.650
coming back to life like zombies...

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:39.510
They, Mr. Takeda's sudoku,
were meant to have beaten you!

00:14:39.510 --> 00:14:40.870
That's right!

00:14:40.870 --> 00:14:44.210
It's hard to imagine him
suddenly being beaten.

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:48.100
Hey, you running away?!

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:50.040
Kaito, wait there!

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:51.730
So, he did run away?

00:14:51.730 --> 00:14:53.660
You've done it, Mr. Takeda!

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:55.590
You won by default!

00:14:55.590 --> 00:14:56.170
What?!

00:14:57.920 --> 00:14:59.190
I never thought...

00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:00.950
this day would come.

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:02.480
Mr. Takeda!

00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:06.230
Naoki!

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:07.430
Yuichi!
Naoki!

00:15:09.310 --> 00:15:11.440
He was only ignoring you, wasn't he?

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:13.440
What?!

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:35.960
Oh, my...

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:38.250
Seems you've made yourself at home.

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:53.090
Sure enough, this feels
all kinds of weird.

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:55.770
Having you here in the POG.

00:15:56.890 --> 00:16:00.790
I feel good havin' gotten
rid of all those layabouts.

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:03.900
For the sake of the Puzzle of God, huh?

00:16:05.850 --> 00:16:08.870
Is this the real you?

00:16:08.870 --> 00:16:09.830
Huh?

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:13.820
You don't seem the same
as the person I knew.

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:17.190
When you see how someone
makes or solves a puzzle,

00:16:17.190 --> 00:16:19.580
you can tell what kind
of person they are.

00:16:21.090 --> 00:16:25.160
You're a lot kinder
than your face lets on.

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:29.430
You think of people bound to you
by puzzles as dear as prizes.

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:31.450
Like people whose skill you acknowledge.

00:16:31.450 --> 00:16:32.880
Kaito Daimon....

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:34.830
Especially him.

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:38.170
You believed that, even if
you did try to kill him,

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:40.640
he'd pull something off somehow.

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:45.860
You had some reason for joining the POG,

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:47.650
one worth betraying your friend for.

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:48.790
Right?

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:53.030
Oh, jeez, I was that transparent?

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:55.030
I knew it.

00:16:55.190 --> 00:16:57.280
You wanted me to say
something like that, huh?

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:02.510
For someone who grew up in
the cutthroat entertainment business,

00:17:02.510 --> 00:17:04.820
you're not too perceptive.

00:17:04.820 --> 00:17:06.560
Erena Himekawa!

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:09.720
You think that guy who can't even eat leeks
would be a friend of mine?

00:17:09.720 --> 00:17:11.800
Don't go talkin' stupid crap.

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:13.220
Leeks?

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:14.490
Kaito Daimon...

00:17:14.490 --> 00:17:16.260
He's just a stepping stone,

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:18.680
in order for me to solve
the Puzzle of God.

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:21.220
I'm gonna crush Kaito, Rook, all of 'em!

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:23.220
Then I'll be the Phi-Brain!

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:25.990
The only one who can do that is someone

00:17:25.990 --> 00:17:28.400
with both Giver and Solver abilities: Me!

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:30.370
I'll prove it to ya:

00:17:30.370 --> 00:17:31.990
That I can solve the ultimate puzzle,

00:17:31.990 --> 00:17:34.400
become the ultimate person!

00:17:37.540 --> 00:17:39.450
That is the real you.

00:17:41.170 --> 00:17:43.700
You've changed, haven't you? For real?

00:17:45.110 --> 00:17:48.560
I used to like the way you laughed.

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:53.170
Okay, fine, sorry for saying
something so stupid.

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:57.800
Keep doing your best,
okay, Mr. Setsu Chido?

00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:59.980
I can't believe it!

00:17:59.980 --> 00:18:01.810
Grabbing hold of a
celebrity's face like that.

00:18:03.150 --> 00:18:04.630
Ah, ah, ah!

00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:07.560
The water bugs are all red, reddy-poo!

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:17.120
Why didn't you say anything?

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:18.950
That you were fighting with Gammon?

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:20.720
Look, just hold that down.

00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:21.910
What's with you?

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:23.460
You're the one who lost to Gammon.

00:18:23.460 --> 00:18:24.660
I didn't lose!

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:28.150
I didn't want to believe it.

00:18:28.150 --> 00:18:30.500
That Gammon had gone over to the POG.

00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:35.560
This is how spacious it
is with no one here, huh?

00:18:35.560 --> 00:18:37.260
This terrace?

00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:40.010
Gammon went over to the POG,

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:42.210
Cube and Ana are gone...

00:18:42.210 --> 00:18:44.310
Why did things come to this?

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:47.810
Why did I see that?

00:18:48.570 --> 00:18:52.310
If I dropped those, I could win.

00:18:52.950 --> 00:18:54.320
But the minute I saw that...

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:56.130
If I'd won, the world would have...

00:18:56.790 --> 00:18:58.060
Wow, it's like...

00:18:58.060 --> 00:19:00.740
I guess I can't help it if even
I'm getting a little gloomy.

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:02.110
So then...

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:03.830
Kaito?

00:19:04.500 --> 00:19:07.230
Those things I saw...

00:19:07.230 --> 00:19:08.270
That was...

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:13.790
The future?

00:19:14.100 --> 00:19:15.660
K..Kaito?

00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:22.440
Why are you eating leeks?

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:40.490
For things to have come to this...

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:44.580
J..Jin!

00:19:58.160 --> 00:19:59.340
What's goin' on?

00:20:00.390 --> 00:20:02.460
Sure enough, the Book of God was not

00:20:02.460 --> 00:20:04.720
meant to fall into human hands.

00:20:06.740 --> 00:20:09.360
That power, which Pythagoras sealed up...

00:20:09.360 --> 00:20:11.600
It is too much for man.

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:21.100
This is what awaits mankind when
the Puzzle of God is solved

00:20:21.100 --> 00:20:24.130
and absolute power obtained.

00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:26.140
The end of the world, eh?

00:20:30.110 --> 00:20:31.450
Don't tell me...

00:20:31.450 --> 00:20:33.560
If the Puzzle of God is solved,

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:34.970
this is what will happen?!

00:20:35.610 --> 00:20:39.840
What I'm seeing really is the future?

00:20:40.110 --> 00:20:44.930
Is this the world that
you wanted, Phi-Brain?!

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:47.190
Tell me, Jin!

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:48.610
Jin!

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:51.100
Jin!

00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:53.270
Kaito!

00:20:55.430 --> 00:20:57.070
What's wrong with you?

00:20:57.070 --> 00:20:58.440
Your face is all pale.

00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:01.190
Kaito?

00:21:01.550 --> 00:21:03.000
What lies ahead...

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:04.960
Oh, no...

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:06.280
Kaito!
Oh, no...

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:07.490
Hey!

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:09.740
Ow!

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:14.850
M..My little toe! Kaito,
I broke my little toe!

00:21:14.850 --> 00:21:16.250
Kaito!

00:21:20.330 --> 00:21:22.920
The Puzzle of God, huh?

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:26.300
You'll get cold out here.

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:29.430
Take this.

00:21:30.150 --> 00:21:32.180
It's the uniform of a POG executive.

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:35.690
Your will, determination, preparedness...

00:21:35.970 --> 00:21:37.750
All these you have shown us.

00:21:38.370 --> 00:21:40.760
We wish to enlist your skill.

00:21:40.760 --> 00:21:43.940
To solve the Puzzle of God, that is.

00:21:45.040 --> 00:21:45.950
Yeah.

00:21:54.340 --> 00:21:56.670
That was the future.

00:21:58.100 --> 00:22:01.760
If that's the world the POG will make

00:22:01.760 --> 00:22:03.760
once they have the Book of God,

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:05.760
I can't let them solve it!

00:22:06.700 --> 00:22:08.050
The Puzzle of God...

00:22:08.320 --> 00:22:09.710
I will solve it!

00:22:14.190 --> 00:22:17.270
The Book of God must not
fall into human hands.

00:22:17.270 --> 00:22:20.480
In order to protect the
world, and the future.

00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:23.730
Isn't that right, Jin?

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:41.540
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:47.340
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:47.770 --> 00:22:52.090
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:52.090 --> 00:22:57.210
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:02.610
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:08.220
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:13.160
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:17.910
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:24.020
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:24.020 --> 00:23:26.600
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:29.250
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:33.910
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:39.180
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:44.400
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:50.050
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:50.050 --> 00:23:58.960
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:03.580 --> 00:24:05.420
This is the end.

00:24:05.810 --> 00:24:07.590
If left on his own any more,

00:24:07.590 --> 00:24:09.170
Kaito will become a different person.

00:24:09.170 --> 00:24:11.170
He'll be unable to solve puzzles?

00:24:11.170 --> 00:24:13.060
Probably, I think so.

00:24:13.060 --> 00:24:14.320
He'll start liking leeks,

00:24:14.320 --> 00:24:16.470
and even say that my
sweets are delicious...

00:24:16.800 --> 00:24:18.430
Hey, wait.

00:24:18.430 --> 00:24:19.890
Wouldn't that Kaito be better?

00:24:19.890 --> 00:24:22.520
Next time, "Glistening Tears"

00:24:22.520 --> 00:24:25.890
That's changing the parts about him
that suits you, isn't it?!
